$ we have ${S}_{2}=[0,\\frac{3}{2}]$\n\n- if $i=3,$ we have ${S}_{3}=[0,\\frac{4}{3}]$\n\nand so on. \n\nNotice that as $i$ increases, \n\n- the left endpoint of the intervals is $0$ for all the sets,\n\n- the right endpoint of the intervals approaches $1$ but never reaches it.\n\nMoreover, all the intervals are contained in ${S}_{1}.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{⋃}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i}={S}_{1}=[0,2].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-174452/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c1e93acb-6c0b-5263-9df9-9dcc00680845"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-174452"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-174449/selection/2531b01062963bf17cb1953367062769d91dcfc4519f4f6b120c5de4951d40dd" :answer/id #uuid "4fcb192e-77e0-51af-a080-dc32995ad0c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "∅" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-174449/selection/9137b828cd574063f061485bc81cba20443d24458e8ff33ddf4201b6045af64f" :answer/id #uuid "5ca71b94-157b-52cf-a62a-e5ebb70f6c6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{0,1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-174449/selection/199bf851613ea946edb4e75e8324794a50da9033dd50c48435253896891f6573" :answer/id #uuid "14a974bd-34df-5539-a51f-b988288577af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-174449/selection/d179684f8ba4dab0968f2a2f8413aef599c5a0b6fd53ebb53f73888f812c82ea" :answer/id #uuid "032132dc-4a4e-5530-b435-c4069330018d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{2i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-174449/selection/d7e016e32ff34495583cf9ed09c94676f755d4c2c7fe7a0983cff62daa5e52b1" :answer/id #uuid "b42b8870-8bbe-5535-90fe-e607e612468e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{0,2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-174449/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b0fc744a-152d-5abc-8b1b-fe24a8313801" :answer-field/key "selection" 